# Non-sensitive tunables for the sensitive stack.
#
# Edit this file, not .env — scripts/render-config.sh regenerates .env from it
# on every `make up STACK=sensitive`. Secrets do NOT belong here; see secrets/README.md.

# The address Caddy binds. 0.0.0.0 on trinity means its one interface on
# Winterfell, 10.0.99.40 — the host is single-homed, so there is nothing else
# it could mean — and the firewall decides who reaches it: Hicks, on the named
# list ADR-0031 records, and nothing from any other segment.
BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0

# The only published port on the tier (ADR-0008, #129). 80 is deliberately not
# published: nothing off-host consumes it (ADR-0012) — a browser on Hicks types
# https, and step-ca's ACME challenge runs over 443 (tls-alpn-01). Publish it
# the day a redirect is wanted, and add the line to compose.yaml's `ports:`
# in the same commit, not before.
HTTPS_PORT=443

# ALLOY_HOSTNAME is deliberately absent — render-config.sh writes it from
# `hostname`, so the agent labels this host as trinity and not as a container
# id. The agent itself is not in this stack: trinity runs one the way oracle
# does, shipped by scripts/deploy-agent.sh, pushing to 10.0.99.20.

# Where Immich keeps the photographs — the originals, the thumbnails, the
# transcodes and its own nightly database dumps, one tree. On trinity this is
# the mount point of the 2 TB USB disk docs/hardware.md assigns to the library,
# formatted ext4 and owned by the deploying user, because immich-server runs
# as ${RENDER_UID} and writes here as nobody else (#404 does the format and
# the chown; compose.yaml says why that uid). The database is NOT under this
# path: it lives in a named volume on the internal SSD, where upstream insists
# a Postgres belongs.
#
# compose.yaml mounts this with create_host_path off, so a missing directory
# is a refused deploy rather than a silently created one on the SSD. An
# EXISTING mount point with nothing mounted on it is the case that cannot be
# caught here, and Immich catches it itself: every subdirectory carries a
# .immich marker written on first start, and a start that cannot read them
# refuses to serve rather than rebuild an empty library on the wrong disk.
IMMICH_UPLOAD_LOCATION=/srv/immich

# The machine-learning container runs by default and sits behind a compose
# profile so that it can be switched off with one line rather than by editing
# compose.yaml: blank this to run without it. #132 asked for the option; the
# ProDesk was chosen (ADR-0034) because 32 GB fits it. If it is off, disable
# machine learning in Administration › Settings as well, or every upload
# queues jobs that fail against a container that is not there.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=ml
